  "term": "mysticism",
  "definition": "Mysticism is a form of religious or speculative thought that claims a direct, immediate experience of the divine or the ultimate basis of existence. In this view, ordinary reflective thought is set aside in favor of a supposed higher, supra-rational union in which the sense of separate individuality may disappear.",
